# Devops/operations properties override file for ds-present.
#
# This is the explicit, per-service override file configured via the 'application-properties-config' Tomcat
# context environment entry (see conf/ocp/ds-present.xml) / Jetty EnvEntry (see src/test/jetty/jetty-env.xml),
# and loaded by ServiceConfig.initializeWithPropertiesOverride(configFile, propertiesOverrideFile). It is meant
# for devops/operations secrets and per-environment values that must never be committed to git.
#
# Copy this file to 'ds-present-application.properties' (same folder, without the '.SAMPLE' suffix) and fill in
# your own values. This filename is already covered by the repository's generic '*-application.properties'
# .gitignore rule.
#
# NOTE: ANY key present in ds-present-behaviour.yaml can be overridden here, using the same dotted/indexed path -
# simple/scalar settings (including indexed lists, e.g. security.realms[0]) AND nested-tree values (imageservers,
# storages, origins, ...) alike, e.g. imageservers[0].example.url or storages[0].main.backends[0].ds-storage.url.
# 'application-config' (see conf/ocp/ds-present.xml) still names exactly one YAML file, identical on every server -
# ServiceConfig writes any override found here back into its in-memory copy of that tree before it is used, rather
# than reading a second YAML file, so the deployed ds-present-behaviour.yaml itself never needs editing. See
# ServiceConfig's class javadoc for how.
#
# The path must match the deployed ds-present-behaviour.yaml's structure exactly, including list position and any
# descriptive key (e.g. the 'example' in 'imageservers[0].example.url' mirrors the '- example:' entry in that
# file) - if that file's structure changes, the matching override keys below must be updated too.
#
# The keys below are the ones commonly set per environment/operator - uncomment and set the ones you need.

# The real image server URL for this environment (see ds-present-behaviour.yaml's 'imageservers' section - the
# entry marked 'default: true' is the one actually used).
# imageservers[0].example.url=https://example.com/devel/iipimage

# The real ds-storage backend URL for this environment (see ds-present-behaviour.yaml's 'storages' section).
# storages[0].main.backends[0].ds-storage.url=http://example.com:9072/ds-storage/v1/

# licensemodule.url=http://example.com:9076/ds-license/v1
# licensemodule.allowall=false

# openapi.serverurl=http://localhost:9073/ds-present/v1

# oldimageserver.url=http://example.com

# security.mode=OFFLINE
# security.baseurl=https://example.com/realms
# security.realms[0]=DS
# security.client.id=changeme
# security.client.secret=changeme
